 s[0] == s[1]:\n        return False\n    for i in range(2, len(s)):\n        if s[i] != s[i-2]:\n            return False\n    return True\n```\n\nThis function first checks if the string length is less than 2, returning `False` in that case. It then verifies that the first two characters are different. For subsequent characters, it ensures each character alternates between the first and second characters by comparing each character to the one two positions back. If all checks pass, it returns `True`.\n</answer>', 
